Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:54:20 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(progress): lesson playback position GET/PUT (v1.8.0,
 schema 1.7.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Blocks the app's "resume from last position". Until now the only persisted
progress was completed/bookmarked lesson ids — nothing stored a timestamp, so
a user who watched half of a lesson and closed the app started over.

New: GET/PUT /lessons/{id}/progress, backed by
wp_mrdastbaaf_lesson_progress (UNIQUE user_id+lesson_id).

Why a table and not usermeta: a position is per-lesson, so usermeta would mean
re-serialising one large JSON blob per user every few seconds during playback
— a heavy write to a shared row, which is the exact pattern behind this
plugin's v1.7.9-1.7.13 suspension incident. Each write here is a small
INSERT ... ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE on a unique key, which also makes two
concurrent PUTs (player + app-background event) idempotent.

Behaviour:
- position is clamped to [0, 86400] and never exceeds duration.
- completed at ceil(duration * 0.95). 100% is unrealistic (credits/trailing
  silence), and duration == 0 never completes — with no duration there is no
  ratio and a false "completed" on the dashboard is worse than none.
- completion is mirrored into completedLessonIds in the same usermeta blob
  GET /me/progress reads, so the player and the dashboard cannot disagree.
- ineffective writes are suppressed: no change or a step under 5s is skipped,
  but a seek, a first real position, and any completion transition are stored.
  A transient 2s open never overwrites real progress, and a sub-5s position
  never creates a row at all (resuming at 2s is worse than starting over).
- PUT without durationSeconds keeps the stored duration instead of zeroing it.
- the response always reports what is actually on the server, plus a `stored`
  flag, so the client can tell a skipped write from an accepted one.

Deliberate decision: this endpoint checks login, not entitlement. Playback
already required a ticket, and a hand-crafted request can only pollute the
caller's own dashboard. Documented in the doc with the condition under which
it should be revisited.

mark_lesson_completed() is a new public method on the memberships controller
rather than a parallel write from the progress controller: the usermeta blob's
shape, sanitisation and 500-item cap belong to that class, and two
implementations would drift. At the cap it drops the oldest entry so the
newest completion is never the one discarded.

Tests: tests/php/test-lesson-progress.php — 33 assertions on clamping, the
completion threshold (including the ceil boundary at 31/33 vs 32/33 and the
zero-duration rule), every branch of the write throttle, and lesson-id
validation including path-traversal shapes. Suite now totals 84 assertions
across three files via tests/php/run-all.sh.

One assertion failed on first run and the test was corrected, not the code:
a 2-second position does not create a row. That is intended, and the test now
documents it explicitly.

Docs: docs/PLUGIN_v1.8.0_PLAYBACK_POSITION.md
