@@ -0,0 +1,179 @@
+# Plugin change — lesson playback position
+
+**Version:** bridge `1.8.0` · **Schema:** `1.6.0` → `1.7.0`
+**Blocks:** the Android app's "resume from last position" feature.
+
+---
+
+## Why
+
+The only persisted progress was *completed* and *bookmarked* lesson ids
+(`PUT /me/progress`). Nothing anywhere stored a timestamp. A user who watched
+half of an hour-long lesson and closed the app started from the beginning next
+time — the server had no idea where they were.
+
+## Storage
+
+```
+wp_mrdastbaaf_lesson_progress
+  id · user_id · lesson_id · position_seconds · duration_seconds
+  completed · updated_at
+  UNIQUE KEY user_lesson_idx (user_id, lesson_id)
+```
+
+**Why a table rather than usermeta.** A position is per-lesson. Storing it in
+usermeta would mean one JSON blob per user, re-serialised and rewritten every few
+seconds during playback — a heavy write to a shared row. That is the exact
+pattern behind this plugin's v1.7.9–v1.7.13 suspension incident. Here each write
+is a small `INSERT … ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE` on a unique key.
+
+`lesson_id` is `varchar(64)`, not `bigint`: the legacy filter path accepted
+non-numeric lesson ids and that contract is preserved.
+
+---
+
+## API contract
+
+### `GET /lessons/{id}/progress` — new
+
+Requires Bearer. Returns the stored position, or a zeroed shape if the lesson was
+never opened.
+
+```jsonc
+{
+  "lessonId": "12",
+  "positionSeconds": 431,
+  "durationSeconds": 1420,
+  "completed": false,
+  "updatedAt": "2026-10-16 12:31:00"     // MySQL local time; null if never watched
+}
+```
+
+Errors: `400 invalid_lesson` (id fails `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$`), `401 unauthorized`.
+
+### `PUT /lessons/{id}/progress` — new
+
+Requires Bearer.
+
+```jsonc
+// Request
+{ "positionSeconds": 431, "durationSeconds": 1420 }
+```
+
+`durationSeconds` is optional. When omitted, the stored duration is kept — a
+request without it would otherwise zero the duration and break the completion
+threshold.
+
+```jsonc
+// 200 — always the state that is actually on the server
+{
+  "lessonId": "12",
+  "positionSeconds": 431,
+  "durationSeconds": 1420,
+  "completed": false,
+  "updatedAt": "2026-10-16 12:31:00",
+  "stored": true
+}
+```
+
+`stored: false` means the write was skipped as ineffective (see below) and the
+returned position is the unchanged stored one. **The client should treat the
+response, not its own request, as the truth.**
+
+Errors: `400 invalid_lesson`, `400 invalid_position` (missing / non-numeric),
+`401 unauthorized`, `500 db_error`.
+
+---
+
+## Behaviour
+
+### Clamping
+
+- position is clamped to `[0, MAX_POSITION_SECONDS]` (86 400 — a sanity cap
+  against a broken client, which would otherwise send a user to the end of a
+  video on resume)
+- **position never exceeds duration**; if a client reports a shorter duration,
+  the position is clamped to it
+
+### Completion
+
+`completed` is set when `position >= ceil(duration × 0.95)`.
+
+95 % rather than 100 % because end credits and trailing silence mean a user
+realistically never reaches the last frame — at 100 % lessons would never be
+marked complete.
+
+**`duration == 0` never completes.** With no duration there is no ratio, and a
+completion flag appearing on the dashboard for an unmeasured lesson is worse than
+no flag.
+
+**Completion is mirrored into `/me/progress`.** When the flag flips to true, the
+lesson id is also appended to `completedLessonIds` in the same usermeta blob that
+`GET /me/progress` and the dashboard read. Without this, the player and the
+dashboard would disagree about what has been finished.
+
+### Write throttling
+
+The player sends a `PUT` every few seconds. Two rules suppress ineffective writes:
+
+| Situation | Stored? |
+|---|---|
+| First real position (≥ 5 s) | ✅ |
+| No change, or a step < 5 s | ❌ |
+| Forward or backward seek ≥ 5 s | ✅ |
+| Crossing the completion threshold, however small the step | ✅ |
+| A transient 2 s open **over** real progress | ❌ — progress is preserved |
+| A position below 5 s when there is no progress yet | ❌ — nothing worth resuming |
+
+The last two are the ones that matter to users: a momentary open must not wipe a
+30-minute position, and a 2-second position must not become the resume point.
+
+---
+
+## Deliberate decision: no entitlement check
+
+This endpoint validates **login**, not **access to the lesson**.
+
+Reasoning:
+
+1. Playback already required a valid ticket, and the position is only sent during
+   that playback flow.
+2. Someone crafting the request by hand can only pollute their own dashboard.
+   They gain no access and touch no other user's data.
+3. The access check is private to the courses controller; exposing it for a
+   cosmetic flag would add coupling for no security benefit.
+
+**Revisit this if lesson completion ever gates something real** — a certificate,
+a score, or a discount.
+
+---
+
+## Tests
+
+`tests/php/test-lesson-progress.php` — 33 assertions, no WordPress required:
+
+```bash
+./tests/php/run-all.sh
+```
+
+Covers clamping (negative, beyond-duration, absurd, zero-duration, non-numeric),
+the completion threshold including the `ceil` boundary (31/33 vs 32/33) and the
+zero-duration rule, every branch of the write throttle, and lesson-id validation
+(including path-traversal shapes and the 64-character column limit).
+
+One assertion initially failed and was corrected rather than the code: a 2-second
+position does **not** create a row. That is intended — resuming at 2 seconds is
+worse than starting over — and the test now documents it explicitly.
+
+Not covered by unit tests: `fetch_row` / `upsert_row` / `handle_put_progress` —
+they need a live `$wpdb`.
+
+## Staging checklist
+
+- [ ] Play a lesson to ~2 minutes, close the app, reopen → `GET /lessons/{id}/progress` returns ~120.
+- [ ] Resume plays from that position.
+- [ ] Open a lesson for 2 seconds → the stored position is **unchanged**.
+- [ ] Watch to the end → `completed: true`, and `GET /me/progress` lists the lesson.
+- [ ] `PUT` without `durationSeconds` → the stored duration is preserved.
+- [ ] Two concurrent `PUT`s (player + app-background event) → exactly one row.
+- [ ] `wp_mrdastbaaf_lesson_progress` exists with `user_lesson_idx` UNIQUE.
